// What a `for` sends from a loop of its body, to other entities and into
// a unique (Inputs/looped_sends.ent, 300,000 entities that each send to
// up to eight others from a `while` and a `for k in a..b`): floats of
// very different sizes, whose sums depend on the order they are added
// in. The order is that of the rows, and for one row that of the loop's
// turns: on one core each value lands where it is sent, on many each
// slice of the rows keeps a list and the lists are combined in order.
// The same either way, with any number of threads.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/looped_sends.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.one
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/looped_sends.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.all
// RUN: env OMP_NUM_THREADS=3 %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/looped_sends.ent 2>/dev/null > %t.three
// RUN: FileCheck %s < %t.one
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.all
// RUN: cmp %t.one %t.three
// Combined in groups, one after another, and whichever has taken less so
// far (devices/sends.c, ENT_COMBINE): the same.
// RUN: env ENT_PARALLEL_MIN=1 %ent build --parallel %S/Inputs/looped_sends.ent -o %t.par
// RUN: env ENT_COMBINE=groups %t.par 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.one
// RUN: env ENT_COMBINE=one %t.par 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.one
// RUN: %t.par 2>/dev/null | cmp - %t.one

// CHECK:      2740.354004 44999950000 146372.140625 599998 1009
// CHECK-NEXT: 7: 0.0019 287834
// CHECK-NEXT: 12345: 0.0 107344
// CHECK-NEXT: 299999: 0.004806 46402
